      "heading": "Care homes, answered",
      "html": "<h3>Is Quickler a care records or eMAR system?</h3><p>No. It does not hold care plans or medication rounds. It writes up your audits and checks. It sits next to your care records system.</p><h3>What can I check in a care home?</h3><p>Safety walks, cleaning audits, fire door checks, equipment checks and incidents. You answer in WhatsApp. The finished Record lands in your list.</p><h3>Does it pass CQC or the Care Inspectorate?</h3><p>No. It gives you dated, photo-backed proof that checks were done. It gives no rating and makes no promise to a regulator.</p><h3>Who owns the data?</h3><p>You do. You are the data controller under UK GDPR and Quickler is your processor. To have Records erased, email hello@quickler.co.</p><h3>Is resident data safe?</h3><p>You choose what your Check asks for. Keep resident detail to the least you need. Quickler handles data under UK GDPR as your processor.</p>"
